 "claims": [
  {
   "id": "K_hook",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "An estimated 2.34 tonnes (gross) of cocaine was found on a fishing boat stranded about 18 km off K'gari, Queensland, on 30 November 2024 (AP: 'a record 2.3 tons of cocaine from a fishing boat'). Narration: 'A fishing boat full of cocaine.' / '2.3 tonnes. Off Australia.' Headline '2.3 TONNES OF COCAINE / ON A FISHING BOAT'.",
   "sources": [
    "afp",
    "ap",
    "nbc",
    "cnn"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "K_pine",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "August 2018: Spanish police seized 67 kg of cocaine hidden in hollowed-out pineapples at Mercamadrid, Madrid's wholesale fruit market; the fruit came from Costa Rica via the Portuguese port of Setubal; seven people arrested (three in Madrid, four in Barcelona). Narration: 'But first, Madrid. Pineapples, stuffed with cocaine.'",
   "sources": [
    "afpwire",
    "local",
    "euronews"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "K_wax",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "Police said the cocaine cylinders were covered in yellow wax to look like pineapple flesh and to mask the drugs' chemical smell. Narration: 'The hole? Sealed with yellow wax.'",
   "sources": [
    "afpwire",
    "local",
    "euronews"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "K_avo",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "April 2025 (Easter weekend): about 80 kg of cocaine was found in about 400 plastic fake avocados delivered to a company in Barendrecht, near Rotterdam; the shipment came from the Dominican Republic; prosecutors said the receiving company is not connected to the drugs. Narration: 'But that was not the weirdest one.' (editorial rehook) / 'Near Rotterdam: 400 avocados. All fake.'",
   "sources": [
    "dutchnews",
    "nltimes",
    "portseu",
    "insight"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "K_drop",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "The fake avocados were discovered when one fell to the ground and broke open. Narration: 'Inside? 80 kilos of cocaine.' / 'One fell and cracked. Real avocados squish.' (the last sentence is an editorial joke).",
   "sources": [
    "dutchnews",
    "nltimes",
    "portseu"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "K_boat",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "Late November 2024: police (AFP, Queensland Police, ABF; long under surveillance per AAP) intercepted a fishing boat off Queensland's Fraser Coast near K'gari. Narration: 'Then Australia, off Queensland.'",
   "sources": [
    "afp",
    "ap",
    "nbc"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "K_mother",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "Police allege the cocaine was transferred to the boat from a larger 'mothership' in international waters (CNN: the recreational fishing boat 'allegedly met a mothership in international waters'; the prosecutor in court, per AAP). Narration: 'Police say it met a mothership at sea.'",
   "sources": [
    "cnn",
    "aap"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "K_break",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "The boat suffered a suspected mechanical breakdown and was stranded about 18 km off the north-eastern tip of K'gari. Narration: 'Then it broke down. Stranded, 18 kilometres out.' Label '18 KM OFF K'GARI'.",
   "sources": [
    "afp",
    "ap",
    "cnn",
    "marex"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "K_bales",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "STATISTIC: police found 51 bales wrapped in roped netting, each holding about 40 kg in 1 kg blocks; estimated gross weight 2.34 tonnes; street value about A$760 million. Narration: '51 bales. 2.34 tonnes.' Counter '2,340 KG'. FUN FACT card '51 BALES / ABOUT 40 KG EACH'.",
   "sources": [
    "afp",
    "nightly",
    "ap",
    "nbc"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "K_record",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "It was then the largest cocaine seizure in Australia's history (AFP; AP), overtaken by the 2.7-tonne Londonderry (Sydney) seizure of June 2026 (AP; NPR). Narration: 'A record, then.'",
   "sources": [
    "afp",
    "ap",
    "ap26",
    "npr26"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "K_punch",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "13 people were charged (AFP; AP). AAP reports two men, aged 17 at the time, pleaded guilty in the Queensland Supreme Court to attempting to possess a commercial quantity of imported drugs; no sentence was found in search as of 18 Oct 2026; the others are accused only. Narration: 'Thirteen were charged. Nobody caught a single fish.' (editorial joke). Label '13 CHARGED'.",
   "sources": [
    "afp",
    "ap",
    "aap"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "K_part3",
   "type": "established",
   "nature": "fact",
   "text": "PART 3 TEASE (end card): March 2017, Spain: police found 57 fake bananas made of resin, stuffed with about 7 kg of cocaine, among real bananas (Valencia and Malaga; two Spanish men charged). End card 'PART 3: 57 FAKE BANANAS MADE OF RESIN'.",
   "sources": [
    "wish",
    "anuk",
    "pbuk"
   ]
  }
 ],
